comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T10:27:23.385Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: every built-in intent now emits resolved budget, measured tokens, within-budget verdict, and degradation; oversized context/next results compact deterministically and all six live tracker probes remained within ceiling."
  "2026-07-30T11:24:13.871Z","harness:codex","Delivery boundary: enforced intent receipts and deterministic degradation are implemented and exact 100% coverage plus token-budget gates pass. The canonical issue remains open until the current-tracker per-intent observed-versus-declared evidence table is published and its negative control is explicitly tied to the release gate."
  "2026-07-30T11:30:54.844Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/829 reviews cohesive SDK context budgets, universal row contracts, bounded graph/health diagnostics, quality ratchets, and exact-head commit e53544cd1."
  "2026-07-30T11:54:22.385Z","harness:codex","Review correction: intent receipts now honor the effective explicit tokenBudget override, and over-budget row sets fall back to a receipt-only envelope instead of dropping rows while retaining stale counts or cursors."
  "2026-07-30T17:13:52.692Z","harness:claude-code","Conformance re-measure 2026-07-30 (evening), at HEAD after the context-budget bundle merged at 14:33Z. Enforcement shipped and works. The three intents this item measured as 43.8x, 19.7x and 2.45x over their declared budgets are now inside them: list triage 1,045 of 1,800 tokens in 6,250 bytes, get inspect 1,208 of 3,200 in 6,565 bytes, search discover 1,300 of 1,800 in 7,219 bytes. The receipt now carries the resolved budget, the measured estimate and the applied degradation, which closes the envelope half of the acceptance criteria.\n\nTwo of this item's own criteria are still open, and one of them is now falsified rather than merely unmet.\n\nThe criterion that list, get and search either declare the budget flag or the intent layer refuses to claim a budget it cannot apply, with no silent third option, is falsified. All three still exit 2 with unknown_option on --token-budget. All three nevertheless claim a budget in the receipt and enforce it at egress. That is precisely the silent third option the criterion forbids: the budget is claimed and applied on a command that offers no way to adjust it. It is reachable today, not latent. pm list --limit 200 --for triage returns budget_receipt_only with zero rows, and pm get <id> --depth deep --for inspect does the same, and neither has any override.\n\nThe criterion that a negative control asserts an intent whose command lacks budget enforcement fails the build is still unmet, and the day showed the control was pointed at the wrong invariant. Enforcement presence was never the fragile part. Reachability of the declared number is, and that is now tracked separately as a blocking dependency on this item, since enforcement cannot honestly be called complete while three of five declared ceilings cannot be met by the commands that declare them.\n\nMethod note for whoever picks this up: measure with the flag on the two commands that accept it. The floor is only visible by raising the ceiling until rows appear. next execute yields nothing at 1200, nothing at 2000, and 1,438 tokens of content at 4000. context orient yields nothing at 2400, nothing at 8000, and 8,417 tokens at 40000."
  "2026-08-01T00:37:51.706Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-08-01: list/get/search now expose --token-budget across CLI, SDK tool options, cursor semantics, contracts, and tool schema 4.3.0. The release gate checks 28 surfaces plus a 256-token infeasible declaration control. Live current-tracker receipts are delivered and within ceiling: context orient 1725/2400 with 11 useful rows; list triage 1703/3200 with 20 rows and a cursor; search discover 1562/1800 with 16 rows; next execute 1109/1200 with 3 ready rows; get inspect 2009/3200. Remaining acceptance before closure: add a generated corpus at least as large as the current tracker to the mandatory gate and a structural negative control that removes enforcement from one declared command."
  "2026-08-01T05:27:12.706Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-08-01: intent enforcement is now measured after projection/compaction, synthesizes resumable terminal continuations, and fails closed when a retained cursor row lacks stable identity. The mandatory quality pipeline executes structural receipt-removal and repeated-metadata negative controls. Current-scale measurements remain within all declared ceilings: context 1000/2400, get 415/3200, list 3181/3200, next 1171/1200, search 1763/1800 estimated tokens. Exact repo coverage is 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-01T06:16:05.960Z","harness:codex","CI follow-up evidence (PR #850): decoded coverage shard 2 and found the real entrypoint test used a developer-machine absolute path, so the executable guard never ran on GitHub Linux or Windows and the assertion waited until timeout. The test now derives the script path from import.meta.url, restoring cross-checkout and cross-platform execution; the ceiling returned from 300s to 120s. Focused validation passes 9/9 in 24.68s, including the real entrypoint in 10.49s; strict ESLint and the complete quality:static chain pass."
  "2026-08-01T06:45:24.586Z","harness:codex","PR #850 review evidence: replaced the stale src/sdk/cli-contracts.ts note with the delivered cross-surface behavior. Numeric SDK tokenBudget and priority inputs now survive Commander normalization, with regression coverage."
  "2026-08-01T13:13:29.360Z","harness:claude-code","Re-measured 2026-08-01 at 2026.8.1. The falsified acceptance criterion recorded on 2026-07-30 is now satisfied on the list family: --token-budget is accepted on list, list-open, list-all, list-closed, get, search, next, context and deps, and is declared in each of their help outputs. It is rejected only when supplied without --for, and the refusal is correct and explains itself: \"--token-budget requires a declared context intent selected with --for\". The earlier reading that list, get and search exit 2 on the flag was taken without --for and is superseded by this measurement.\n\nConformance on the list family is now good rather than absent. On 330 open items: budget 1200 gives 12 rows, estimated_tokens 1145, budget_derived_limit 12; budget 3000 gives 38 rows, estimated_tokens 3190. Plain list --json for comparison is 74,457 bytes. The 43.8x divergence recorded for list:triage on 2026-07-30 is gone, and no result is omitted.\n\nTwo residuals, both routed rather than re-filed here. The budget stops binding above the default page cap and the derived-limit field is omitted exactly when the clamp applies; that is the new ceiling item. The emitted payload divided by four exceeds estimated_tokens by roughly seven percent at every budget measured, in the same direction; that belongs to the accounting item."
